				\begin{document}$$\frac{\partial \left({\Delta G}^{*}\right)}{\partial p}>0$$\end{document}∂ΔG∗∂p>0, pressure will increase the activation energy for nucleation. Because the crystallization of Li4PS4I is exothermic, see Figure S4 (with ΔG < 0), this implies a molar volume change of ΔV > 0. Although somewhat uncommon, the glassy 1.5Li2S–0.5P2S5–LiI may indeed be more dense, as the tetragonal Li4PS4I phase contains five crystallographic Li sites with an occupation of < 50% on average and therefore a large fraction of “free volume”. At the same time, however, we cannot fully rule out that the crystallization is kinetically hindered for the reason mentioned above.Figure 5
Reaction scheme for the preparation of Li4PS4I from glassy 1.5Li2S–0.5P2S5–LiI. In contrast to ambient pressure conditions with EA1, an increase in activation energy (nucleation barrier) EA2 is noticed when the synthesis is performed under pressure.
